# Required Sections

Navbar

Sticky positioned. Transparent or minimal styling at the top of the page. Switches to a solid/blurred background with a soft shadow once the user scrolls past a small threshold. Drive the scroll state through a signal (e.g. a scroll-position signal updated via a passive scroll listener) and bind the template to that signal — never mutate the DOM directly outside Angular's reactivity.

Hero

About

Services

Why Choose Us

Statistics

Testimonials

Contact Form

Footer

---

# Contact Form

The contact form should use

Typed Reactive Forms

Validation

Accessible labels

Meaningful error messages

On successful submission

Show a success pop-up modal, reusing the shared Modal component.

Update the URL to /done using Angular Router (Router.navigate or RouterLink), without a full page reload.

The /done route may render the success confirmation as a routed "modal" view (styled as a centered dialog over a dimmed backdrop) so the pop-up and the URL change are satisfied by one flow, not two duplicated UIs.

