# Delivery & Submission

GitHub Repository

Two branches are required.

master

Contains the full source code.

Second branch (e.g. gh-pages)

Contains a static production build for a live demo hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub Pages only serves static files — it cannot run the Node/Express SSR server used for the primary deployment. This branch must be built as a static/prerendered export (SSG or CSR, with base-href adjusted for the repo name), kept separate from the SSR artifact deployed elsewhere.

README.md

Replace the default Angular CLI README before submission. It must explain

- Project setup and how to run the app locally
- How Server-Side Rendering (SSR) is implemented
- How Zoneless Change Detection was applied

Live URL

Deploy the SSR build to Vercel, Netlify, or Firebase to verify SSR behavior and Lighthouse performance. This is separate from the static GitHub Pages branch above.

